# Postgres connection strings. Locally, point both at the same database
# (e.g. a free Neon project, or a local `postgres` instance).
#
# On Vercel: add the "Neon" or "Vercel Postgres" integration from the
# Storage tab — it auto-populates DATABASE_URL / DIRECT_URL (or similarly
# named vars you copy across) as Environment Variables for you.
#
# DATABASE_URL should be the pooled ("...-pooler..." / pgbouncer) connection
# string — used by the app at runtime, across many serverless invocations.
# DIRECT_URL should be the direct (non-pooled) connection string — used only
# for `prisma db push` / `prisma migrate`, since some DDL operations aren't
# supported through a pooled/pgbouncer connection.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"
